id: pm-xq09zu
title: Investigate unmatched aggregate starts from automation telemetry on 2026.10.24
description: "A complete remote telemetry join found four aggregate command_start rows from producer2026.10.24 and source_context automation since2026-10-25T19:20:00Z with no matching command_finish by installation/session/command after more than two minutes. Current broker queue is empty and the required reliability threshold gate passes. Termination, timeout, producer lifecycle and ingestion causes remain unverified; this is an investigation rather than a confirmed current-version defect."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T19:40:57.328Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T16:22:51.510Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Identify the producing automation and whether termination or ingestion explains each unmatched start; Reproduce any confirmed lifecycle defect with isolated positive and negative controls; Preserve sampling and distinguish intentional interruption from missing finalization without fabricating success
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: Identify why each of the four 2026.10.24 automation aggregate starts lacks a matching finish; record termination evidence or a reproducible defect with a canonical owner and paired lifecycle controls.
actual_result: "Latest complete bounded installation audit through2026-10-27T11:27:56.303Z, from08:41:00Z:143starts/142finishes, exactly one unequal history group at09:23:31.637UTC, independently re-read. All seven native history-reader processes in the original closure audit exited0; actual causation remains unproven. Fresh11:23UTC history start/finish ingestion0.738039/0.601494seconds and Sentry pm history root27.091ms are visible; span attribute enrichment is unavailable. Required observability gate passes at5.51percent errors<=6 with zero missing codes or blocking Sentry issues. Client event/OTLP queues are empty; last broker snapshot has0ready/1unacknowledged message, so no global drainage claim. Earlier post-source10/9,82/81 checkpoints, older388/387 changelog window and original four2026.10.24 starts remain separate unresolved observations. No synthetic terminal event or lifecycle repair."
